* Goal\nRelease escrowed assets\nto an attacker address
** Obtain a valid\nthreshold of signatures
*** Steal keys from signer hosts\n(phishing, lateral movement)\n= Ronin 2022
*** Backdoor the node binary\nvia the build pipeline\n= Poly Network 2023
*** Abuse delegated signing\nauthority never revoked\n= Ronin 2022
*** Capture signer-set governance\nand add attacker keys
** Corrupt what the\nattestor believes
*** Poison the RPC nodes the\nattestor reads\n= Kelp DAO 2026
*** DDoS the honest sources so\nfailover lands on poisoned ones\n= Kelp DAO 2026
*** Answer honestly to monitoring\nand falsely to the attestor\n= Kelp DAO 2026
** Make the threshold\ntrivially satisfiable
*** Uninitialised threshold\ndefaults to zero\n= Ronin 2024
*** Application requires a single\nverifier, or a default it never read\n= Kelp DAO 2026
*** Malicious upgrade lowers\nthe required weight
*** Duplicate signatures from one\nkey counted separately
** Bypass proof verification
*** Zero-length Merkle witness\nwith attacker-chosen root\n= Dedaub finding
*** Replay a valid proof on a\nsecond chain or a second time
*** Attest to origin state that\nwas never finalised
** Attack the escrow directly
*** Upgrade the escrow\nimplementation and drain it
*** Accounting drift from\nfee-on-transfer or rebasing
*** Direct donation inflates\nunlockable balance
